BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (  In the ancient days, two rivers flowed through a barren valley-the River of First Trust and th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (    e River of Reciprocity. Each was governed by a spirit, and both spirits possessed magical wa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (    ters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (  The First Spirit held five golden vessels each dawn. She could pour any amount into the valley) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (     between them, and the waters would triple as they flowed toward the Second Spirit. But the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (    Second Spirit alone decided what waters to return upstream, defying nature itself.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (  For many seasons, fear ruled. The First Spirit hoarded her vessels, and the Second Spirit rece) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    ived nothing. The valley remained barren, and both spirits grew weaker.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (  One day, the First Spirit poured generously, trusting in balance. The waters tripled and flowe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (    d abundantly to the Second Spirit. Moved by this faith, the Second Spirit returned half the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (    blessing upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (  Both spirits flourished. The more the First Spirit trusted, the more flowed between them. The ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    more the Second Spirit honored this trust, the more both prospered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (  Soon the valley bloomed eternal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (  The ancient lesson remains: **Abundance flows from trust given and trust honored. When we pour) Tj ET
