BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  # The Parable of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  In an ancient land, two villages sat on opposite sides of a sacred mountain. Each had a mystic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    al well: the Well of Giving and the Well of Receiving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  The gods decreed a covenant: whatever water was poured into the Well of Giving would flow thro) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    ugh the mountain, tripling in volume, before emerging in the Well of Receiving. The receiver) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (     could then decide how much to send back through hidden streams.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  At first, the villages were cautious. They sent mere drops, receiving trickles in return. Both) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (     remained thirsty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  One season, a brave elder named Solara poured generously into the Well of Giving, trusting the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (     distant village. The water tripled, flowing abundantly to the other side. The receivers, mo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    ved by this faith, returned a worthy portion - not all, for they too needed sustenance, but ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    enough to honor the gift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (  Solara's people drank deeply. The cycle continued.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (  The villages learned: when both give with open hands and return with grateful hearts, the sacr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (    ed multiplication blesses all. Greed breaks the covenant - hoarding the tripled waters poiso) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.0 Tf 48.0 24.0 Td (Page 5 of 285) Tj ET
Q
