BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (      # The Parable of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (      In an ancient land, two villages sat on opposite sides of a sacred mountain. Each had a my) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (        stical well: the Well of Giving and the Well of Receiving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      The gods decreed a covenant: whatever water was poured into the Well of Giving would flow ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (        through the mountain, tripling in volume, before emerging in the Well of Receiving. The ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (        receiver could then decide how much to send back through hidden streams.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      At first, the villages were cautious. They sent mere drops, receiving trickles in return. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        Both remained thirsty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      One season, a brave elder named Solara poured generously into the Well of Giving, trusting) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (         the distant village. The water tripled, flowing abundantly to the other side. The recei) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (        vers, moved by this faith, returned a worthy portion - not all, for they too needed sust) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (        enance, but enough to honor the gift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      Solara's people drank deeply. The cycle continued.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      The villages learned: when both give with open hands and return with grateful hearts, the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        sacred multiplication blesses all. Greed breaks the covenant - hoarding the tripled wate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (        rs poisons future flows. But balanced reciprocity transforms scarcity into abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      Thus the mountain taught: trust multiplies resources; fair return sustains trust; together) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        , both villages flourish.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    reasoning:) Tj ET
