BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (    # The Parable of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    In an ancient land, two villages sat on opposite sides of a sacred mountain. Each had a myst) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      ical well: the Well of Giving and the Well of Receiving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    The gods decreed a covenant: whatever water was poured into the Well of Giving would flow th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      rough the mountain, tripling in volume, before emerging in the Well of Receiving. The rece) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      iver could then decide how much to send back through hidden streams.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    At first, the villages were cautious. They sent mere drops, receiving trickles in return. Bo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      th remained thirsty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    One season, a brave elder named Solara poured generously into the Well of Giving, trusting t) Tj ET
