BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      # The Tale of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      In the ancient days, two rivers flowed through a barren valley-the River of First Trust an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        d the River of Reciprocity. Each was governed by a spirit, and both spirits possessed ma) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (        gical waters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      The First Spirit held five golden vessels each dawn. She could pour any amount into the va) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        lley between them, and the waters would triple as they flowed toward the Second Spirit. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        But the Second Spirit alone decided what waters to return upstream, defying nature itsel) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        f.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      For many seasons, fear ruled. The First Spirit hoarded her vessels, and the Second Spirit ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        received nothing. The valley remained barren, and both spirits grew weaker.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      One day, the First Spirit poured generously, trusting in balance. The waters tripled and f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        lowed abundantly to the Second Spirit. Moved by this faith, the Second Spirit returned h) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        alf the blessing upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      Both spirits flourished. The more the First Spirit trusted, the more flowed between them. ) Tj ET
