BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    Myth: In the Valley of Echoes, after three barren seasons of mutual silence, the Spirit of D) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      awn faced a choice.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    "The mists may have deceived us both," she said to the ancient Guardians. "Each of us holds ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      our truth fiercely. Each believes we were the one who risked and was betrayed. This certai) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      nty keeps us both starving.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    "What if," she continued slowly, "I act not from certainty but from humility? Not abandoning) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (       my memory of what happened, but acknowledging the mists might distort all our perceptions) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      ?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    The Guardians watched as she selected two stones-not five, not three like before, but two. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (       genuinely careful step.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    "This is different from before," the Guardian of Memory observed. "Before, you sent stones t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      o break silence. Now you send stones while admitting you might not see clearly.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (    The Spirit of Dawn nodded. "If the Spirit of Dusk returns fairly from these six stones, perh) Tj ET
