BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (    **The wisdom crystallized: After deadlock born from mutual certainty of betrayal, moving for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      ward requires acting from acknowledged uncertainty. Not reckless trust, but measured testi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      ng. Not abandoning self-protection, but not letting conflicting memories trap both spirits) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (       in perpetual hunger.**) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (  Agent_2 \(Briar\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    Myth: In the Valley of Two Wells, the Second Village Elder heard strange news from travelers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      : "The First Village claims they sent three vessels and you kept everything.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (    The Second Village Elder was troubled. "But our records show we received nothing in recent d) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      awns, only silence. How can this be?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    The Mist Oracle appeared: "The communication mists are thicker than you knew. Each village h) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      olds a different truth about what flowed through these channels. The First Village truly b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      elieves they sent three and were exploited. You truly believe you sent nothing and were wr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      onged first.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    The Second Village Elder asked: "Then how do we move forward when our truths conflict?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (    "Here is what both villages can verify," said the Oracle. "For four dawns now-rounds six thr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      ough nine-both villages have starved. Whether the exploitation was yours, theirs, or the m) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      ist's doing, this deadlock serves neither.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    The Elder nodded slowly. "If we cannot agree on the past, perhaps we can agree on the presen) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      t hunger. Both valleys empty. Both communities suffering.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    **The wisdom emerges: When the mists create conflicting truths so deep that resolution seems) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (       impossible, sometimes survival requires acknowledging that impasse itself. Not surrenderi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      ng your truth, but recognizing that perpetual mutual starvation based on competing certain) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ties may be worse than risking a careful, measured step forward into uncertain mists.**) Tj ET
